WEBVTT

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:03.650
Get the camera back on the match.
Front and center.

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:06.480
Broadcast Van

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:06.470
Get one on the reader, too. That's it.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:08.810
Zoom in on each player.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:11.050
Master first, then challenger.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:16.240
I don't know much about karuta,

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:21.230
but I know this is a really 
important, critical stage.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:31.590
<i>and allow us this secret rendezvous</i>

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.840
<i>bring a life of everlasting love</i>

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:47.140
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.970
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:56.050
Verse 20

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:56.050
May the 
scarlet 
kadsuras

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.290
I can't believe Harada-san 
has the Master in check!

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:57.050
Just one more card, and he'll 
have the three wins he needs.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.760
Even if he loses, there's still the fifth match.

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:01.350
The Master's got his back to the wall.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.760
Is Suo-kun finally going down?

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:07.800
What a relief! That weirdo 
was such a headache.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.140
But then again...

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:16.390
There's no doubt Master Harada 
would be quite a headache, too...

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:18.110
<b>Now that I have this,
I'm not giving it to anyone!!</b>

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:26.330
<i>The only cards left are "Since I," "As my,"</i>

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:29.770
<i>"May the time we," "May the time 
spent," and "May the scarlet."</i>

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:35.140
<i>Think hard.</i>

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:37.820
<i>I definitely have a feeling that</i>

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:41.220
<i>bring a life of everlasting love</i>

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:40.430
<i>the "May the time spent" 
I sent to Suo-kun won't be read.</i>

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:41.230
<i>But...</i>

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:44.010
<i>and allow us this secret rendezvous</i>

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:44.010
<i>The "May the scarlet" that I still have...</i>

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:46.530
<i>May the scarlet kadsuras...</i>

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:52.170
<i>...is the card I took to win our 
luck-of-the-draw in the first match.</i>

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:55.270
<i>Would the same thing happen twice?</i>

00:02:55.270 --> 00:03:07.910
<i>Minister of the Right Sanjo 
May the scarlet kadsuras of Mount Afusaka live up to their name and allow us this secret rendezvous</i>

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:58.340
<i>It's the card known as the Master's card</i>

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:59.280
<b>Master</b>

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:01.830
<i>because it contains the two characters 
in the word for "Master."</i>

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:07.340
<i>Is my desire to be the Master
making me believe that it will be read?</i>

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:12.610
<i>And "May the time spent" and 
"May the time we" aside,</i>

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:19.340
<i>could Master Suo recognize "May the scarlet"
 on the "the" and come after it?</i>

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:23.120
Excuse me.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.480
<b>Swoosh...</b>

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:32.980
<b>Gulp</b>

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:37.670
<i>That thing Dr. Harada used 
to do all the time...</i>

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.570
<b>Gulp</b>

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:40.580
<i>I've been through a lot 
of things in my life.</i>

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:44.330
<i>Of course I have a lot to think about.</i>

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:46.920
<i>He seriously has no regard 
for the rules at all!</i>

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:47.820
<i>What a disgrace!</i>

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:55.790
<i>bring a life of everlasting love</i>

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:50.560
<i>It's in karuta's nature 
to have a lot going on.</i>

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:53.160
<i>No matter what kind of feeling I have,</i>

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:57.840
<i>and allow us this secret rendezvous</i>

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:57.440
<i>either card is just as likely to 
be read in a luck-of-the-draw.</i>

00:03:58.160 --> 00:03:59.820
Sorry about that.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:05.910
<i>So let's just take all of it in...</i>

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.940
<i>and have a good time here,</i>

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:10.260
<i>Suo-kun.</i>

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:22.680
<i>I beseech them to wait for the 
Emperor's return before falling</i>

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:29.110
<i>Since I could not hide my love,</i>

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:28.680
<i>Dead card...</i>

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:29.670
<i>The Master...</i>

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:31.560
<i>didn't even move.</i>

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.480
<i>But what...</i>

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.260
<i>did I just sense coming this way?</i>

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:40.250
Taichi, Taichi. I think we can
move up to the front.

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:42.250
There's some space.

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:45.250
<i>Harada has the advantage with his two wins?</i>

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:47.580
<i>Does he really?</i>

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:50.600
<i>Given his physical condition, he might 
not make it through a fifth match.</i>

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:53.260
<i>He's the one with his back to the wall!</i>

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.400
<i>If he doesn't take the win here,</i>

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.560
<i>his chances of becoming the Master are...</i>

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:01.840
<i>As my love first...</i>

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:03.660
<i>Again... the Master didn't move.</i>

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:06.900
<i>How can he be so calm about this?</i>

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.070
<i>Is he that confident in his hearing?</i>

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:12.180
<i>Still, he's moving this way.</i>

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:14.070
<i>His heart...</i>

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:17.460
<i>and allow us this secret rendezvous</i>

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:17.450
<i>His heart is with this card.</i>

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:24.050
<i>and allow us this secret rendezvous</i>

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:24.040
<i>This must mean I'm not the only 
one fixated on being the Master.</i>

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:35.600
<i>It's me.</i>

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:38.990
Being on the receiving end of 
that help makes me stronger!

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:41.810
<i>It has to be me.</i>

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:43.480
<i>and allow us this secret rendezvous</i>

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:45.330
<i>May the...</i>

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:53.610
<i>...time we spend apart from one another be</i>

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:57.620
<i>and allow us this secret rendezvous</i>

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.630
<i>Fault...</i>

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:03.160
The winner of the fourth Master match,
 by two cards, is Master Suo.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:05.630
<i>That was close!</i>

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:06.620
<i>Harada-san almost had it!</i>

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:08.840
<i>I can't believe he faulted...</i>

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:12.890
<i>Did Suo-san actually... now, of all times...</i>

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:19.280
<i>use his usual style and lure 
Dr. Harada into messing up?</i>

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:35.370
<i>Attendant to Empress Koka 
May the time spent in our
one night together bring 
a life of everlasting love</i>

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:35.370
<i>Minister of the Right Sanjo 
May the scarlet kadsuras
 of Mount Afusaka live up 
to their name and allow us
 this secret rendezvous</i>

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:32.130
<i>Card 99 was "May the scarlet,"</i>

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:34.570
<i>and card 100 was "May the time spent"...</i>

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.620
<i>This is what it came down to?</i>

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:50.260
<i>and allow us this secret rendezvous</i>

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:43.380
<i>Harada-san is to be commended for guessing 
that "May the scarlet" would come first,</i>

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:50.260
<i>bring a life of everlasting love</i>

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:47.300
<i>as is the Master for knowing he would 
lose if he simply protected his card</i>

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.250
<i>and turning the situation around.</i>

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:54.010
The fifth match will begin 
in twenty minutes.

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:55.890
Twenty minutes?

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:58.050
Can Dr. Harada's knees handle that?

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:00.760
I'm going out for some fresh air.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:07.270
Shinobu!

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:10.510
It's time for your interview 
about defending your title!

00:07:10.510 --> 00:07:13.630
What are you doing? And you 
still have your tasuki on!

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:20.280
You can just give them a 
quick greeting like always.

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:22.540
What happened in the Master match?

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:23.780
I'm not sure...

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:26.290
Numbered tickets for the fifth 
match are distributed here.

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:30.350
If they're having a fifth match, 
that means the Master won.

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:32.260
Where were you even looking, Mom?

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:34.000
I don't care about that.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.100
And I know you don't, either.

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:42.030
Goodness, what an unsightly tasuki.

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:45.360
Let's make sure you have 
a proper one next time.

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:01.620
<i>Why...</i>

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:05.140
<i>Why couldn't I have been born male?</i>

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:09.710
<i>I want... I want to teach him a lesson.</i>

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:11.340
<i>I want to beat him.</i>

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:14.790
<i>I can't accept the fact that
someone like him is the Master!</i>

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:18.620
<i>The idea that he's the strongest person</i>

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:21.110
<i>in the entire world of the karuta I love!</i>

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:25.590
<i>Now, let's hear Wakamiya-san's 
impressions of the Queen match,</i>

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:27.700
<i>where she just defended her title.</i>

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:30.070
<i>Congratulations!</i>

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:31.560
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:35.440
You did drop your first ever round
 in a Queen match.

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:36.700
That's true.

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:40.570
Another mindless comment with 
no thought put into it!

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:43.660
I'll never forget her comments 
after playing Yumin!

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:49.670
<i>Inokuma Haruka-san has a strength that 
makes me glad I played against her.</i>

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:54.880
That one loss was tough...

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:01.940
But it's like you announcers always say.

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:02.690
Huh?

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:05.790
Every victory is thanks to 
the people beside you.

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:08.970
You've said that every year yourself...

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:10.440
I was just winging it.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.440
Huh?!

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:15.800
This year, I did feel a bit like I won 
because of who was beside me.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:24.780
I'm kind of looking forward to 
next year's Queen match.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:30.190
Let's play karuta again!

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:31.530
When?

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:32.990
The Queen match!

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.820
<i>The one I have to fight</i>

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:46.240
<i>is the one other player who's the 
strongest in the world of the karuta I love.</i>

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:48.430
<i>That's all.</i>

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:51.060
<i>That's all I need!</i>

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:52.950
Chihaya?

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:54.560
<i>As for the Master,</i>

00:10:00.790 --> 00:10:02.500
<i>I can leave him to...</i>

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:09.260
Arata?!

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:09.880
Don't you have a cold?

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:10.890
I do!

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:15.600
Are you okay? Shouldn't you be resting?

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:21.900
I came to ask you, Chihaya...

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:24.130
for your answer.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:25.870
My answer?

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:29.670
I can't... I can't answer you yet, Arata.

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:33.640
Damn it, Arata, don't sneak 
around behind my back!

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:36.650
Where's Dr. Harada?!

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:37.640
Sleeping in his green room!

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:38.410
Wanna go?!

00:10:41.650 --> 00:10:43.170
Sob, sob...

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:47.330
Master 
Suo
Hisashi's 
Green
Room

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:07.890
<b>He finally finished them!!</b>

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.380
Anyone have a hair tie?

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:16.270
Huh?

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:17.120
Uh...

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:18.320
I do!

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:20.690
Thanks.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:22.930
I'm using the washroom, too.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:28.620
Challenger 
Harada 
Hideo's 
Green 
Room

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:41.560
There are plenty of numbered tickets 
left for the Urayasu room.

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:42.980
I'll watch it downstairs.

00:11:42.980 --> 00:11:44.910
But why? You came all this way.

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:45.930
I mean—

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:53.210
I'll watch it downstairs.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:57.700
How do you think the fifth match will go?

00:11:57.700 --> 00:12:00.480
It depends on Dr. Harada's 
condition and spirit.

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:01.540
And his knees...

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:05.300
If the Master plays lazily,
like he did in the first two matches...

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:07.530
<b>Omi Jingu</b>

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:11.490
Competitors, please assemble in the hall.

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:24.800
Master
 Tournament 
Fifth 
Match

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:24.800
Final Round

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:30.840
You look a lot younger 
without the whiskers.

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:34.410
I forgot you were only 26.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:37.230
I envy you.

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:52.650
<i>Five matches in ten hours, 
starting at 10:00 AM...</i>

00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:57.270
<i>Even the people who were just 
watching started to burn out</i>

00:12:57.270 --> 00:12:59.580
<i>as the cards were read one after another,</i>

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.300
<i>but Dr. Harada never gave up.</i>

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:08.500
Master Suo looks quite 
different from earlier.

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:11.270
Fifth Match Commentary

00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:10.670
Part of it is that he's shaved, but also...

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:14.050
I don't like this at all.

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:21.570
Is the Master gonna run away with the win?
The Master's finally getting serious in the fifth match?! 
The Master looks like a different person now!!
What'll happen? Who's gonna win?? 
Don't lose, bear!     So polite... 
Harada-saaaaaan! Don't loooooose!!     Good luck, Master

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:17.550
Impolite guys aren't scary.

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:20.580
They'll always get careless.

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:21.560
But...

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:25.650
People who behave politely 
are harder to deal with.

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:28.500
A show of respect is also a show of fear.

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:32.160
Suo-kun won't be showing Harada 
any further weakness.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:34.660
What's the differential now?     What'd he do with his whiskers lolol 
The Master's so fast 
Is he finally gonna finish this now?

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:34.650
Just look at his bearing.

00:13:35.390 --> 00:13:40.660
It looks like Harada has made
the Master truly be the Master.

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:44.980
<i>It's not over yet.</i>

00:13:44.980 --> 00:13:48.670
<i>I still have a chance. If I just 
play each card carefully...</i>

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:55.520
<i>I'll get closer than anyone 
to where you currently are!</i>

00:13:55.990 --> 00:14:00.330
<i>What kind of karuta will you play in 
the last stages of the fifth match?</i>

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:02.030
<i>I'll figure it out!</i>

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:04.980
<i>Dr. Harada...</i>

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:07.230
<i>You can't.</i>

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:10.290
<i>Dr. Harada, I...</i>

00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:13.840
<i>What sort of person are you?</i>

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:16.240
<i>What can you do, and what can't you do?</i>

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:20.930
<i>I got hurt by Suo-san's words,</i>

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:23.710
<i>so I ran and tattled to you about his eyes.</i>

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:28.360
<i>Every thought of Suo-san has been 
accompanied by dark feelings.</i>

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:31.970
Harada, grade 6, is playing well.

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:34.460
He's really hanging in there.

00:14:34.460 --> 00:14:36.350
<i>Rain takes longer...</i>

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:38.110
Harada, grade 6, defended 
a one-syllable card!

00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:42.260
<i>Did you think I wouldn't notice?</i>

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:44.390
<i>You reacted on "-in takes."</i>

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:50.060
<i>When you start to get tired, 
your game sense falters.</i>

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:58.660
<i>If only I were still young, too...</i>

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:05.970
<i>Dr. Harada is facing every 
moment of this fight head-on.</i>

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:08.960
<i>But it's fine.</i>

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:15.040
<i>Someone young will take 
what's happened today...</i>

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:15.720
<i>I long for the agony I feel now</i>

00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:19.700
Thank you very much.

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:22.460
<i>...and make it work for them.</i>

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:30.870
The winner of the fifth match, 
by twelve cards, is Master Suo.

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:36.210
With three wins and two losses, 
Master Suo has defended his title.

00:15:39.760 --> 00:15:42.590
So the Master is still Suo-kun...

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:44.350
That really kept me on edge, though.

00:15:44.350 --> 00:15:47.040
But the Master's retiring now, right?

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:48.270
That's a relief.

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:52.040
<i>A relief... That's true.</i>

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:57.570
<i>Even Dr. Harada's tenacity
couldn't knock him off his throne.</i>

00:15:58.540 --> 00:15:59.310
<i>He'd better...</i>

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:02.700
<i>become a legend of the past sooner than later.</i>

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:07.020
You must be tired after all that, dear.

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:12.030
Well... yeah. I'm tired, all right.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:17.500
Sorry, I couldn't become the Master.

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:19.290
I don't need any of that.

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:24.040
<b>Shock</b>

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:24.030
I've never once wished for that.

00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:29.740
What I wanted was to see you smile.

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:31.440
Nothing more.

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:36.550
We will now interview the Master.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:39.180
Congratulations on your 
fifth consecutive win.

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:40.800
Thank you.

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:43.260
Your win streak was snapped today,

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:46.250
and you were taken all the way
to the final round.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:47.520
How do you feel?

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:52.570
I'm tired.

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:55.570
And your impressions after 
facing Harada-san?

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.080
I'm tired.

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:01.820
Um, can you be more specific?

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:07.280
<i>It was fun.</i>

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:11.080
<i>Playing karuta was fun.</i>

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:21.380
<i>It was fun.</i>

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:25.940
You declared that you would retire 
after your fifth consecutive win.

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:27.840
Is that still how you feel?

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:34.860
Just be sure to make 
something of yourself.

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:37.040
Yes...

00:17:38.210 --> 00:17:39.610
It is.

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:41.490
My retirement—

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:42.210
Master!

00:17:44.030 --> 00:17:45.240
You... Wait a—

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:46.160
Master!

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:52.010
What are you doing, Wataya-kun?! Come on!

00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:52.560
Wait!

00:17:52.560 --> 00:17:54.870
He's being interviewed! 
It's a live broadcast!

00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:55.940
But... Master...

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:56.330
Master...

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:57.590
Suo-san!

00:17:57.590 --> 00:17:58.660
Wataya-kun!

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:00.150
Don't quit, Suo-san!

00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:01.560
Don't quit!

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:02.720
Stay the Master!

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:08.430
I'll come here to beat you!

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:21.390
Okay. I'll give you one 
more year... for free.

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.240
<b>Gasp</b>

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:25.750
<b>...still in it!     For real?     Wooooow     For free? 
For free lolol     Oooooh 
Who's the kid?     Aaaaaand he's still in the game 
Is this a shonen manga now?</b>

00:18:58.530 --> 00:18:59.990
So it's finally over.

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:03.810
Thanks for everything, Sakurazawa-san.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:05.780
I didn't do anything.

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:11.750
I really think the baby 
inside me now is a girl.

00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:14.760
I prayed to god earlier.

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:18.680
"Even if it means I have a boy,
please let me win."

00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:21.390
If you want to call it silly,
just don't say anything.

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:25.140
You can't imagine the resolve it takes
to be a mother of three boys.

00:19:27.260 --> 00:19:28.950
But since I lost...

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:32.890
my challenge ends here.

00:19:32.890 --> 00:19:35.480
My, Inokuma-san! You're expecting?

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:36.760
Your third?

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:38.680
Are you feeling all right?

00:19:38.680 --> 00:19:42.910
Goodness, dear, you pushed yourself 
so hard! You're so tough!

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:44.790
Yes, I guess I managed...

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:47.960
So will you be going on 
maternity leave again?

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:51.530
My, you will certainly be busy!

00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:53.420
I'm not sure I'll make it back, though...

00:19:56.330 --> 00:20:00.410
I thought so when the Queen 
lost the second match too,

00:20:01.390 --> 00:20:04.120
but when you get to be my age,

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:09.630
when a young person stops and stands still, 
you see it as them planting a seed.

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:14.750
From my perspective, you are still young.

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:17.920
You will come back.

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:35.730
Quick! Hurry up!

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:38.200
If we miss the next Nozomi, 
we won't get home until really late!

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:40.880
Wait! Food! Souvenirs!

00:20:40.160 --> 00:20:42.580
You can buy those on the train!

00:20:43.070 --> 00:20:45.820
Man, what an intense day this was.

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:47.590
I'm exhausted just from watching.

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:50.190
I feel bad for Dr. Harada,

00:20:50.190 --> 00:20:54.360
but so much crazy stuff happened,
 like the Master calling off his retirement!

00:20:57.530 --> 00:20:59.320
Chow time!

00:20:58.520 --> 00:20:59.690
!noos ooT

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:00.360
You're eating that already?

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:02.760
Yep. I'm gonna eat one at 
each station we stop at.

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:03.950
The first one's for Kyoto!

00:21:04.350 --> 00:21:06.630
Wait, why isn't Taichi here?

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:08.770
He was with us at the station...

00:21:10.030 --> 00:21:11.400
Did he miss the train?!

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:12.220
Goof.

00:21:11.400 --> 00:21:12.610
Goof, indeed.

00:21:12.610 --> 00:21:13.210
Actually...

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:15.510
He told me earlier.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:20.450
He's staying behind to play in the 
Takamatsu Memorial Cup tomorrow.

00:21:23.280 --> 00:21:26.940
<i>Taichi's getting the jump on me!</i>
